{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "Peter's Graduation", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Goodbye and Good Luck", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 11, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 13, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A2.2", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Identify and describe plans for the organization of events.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations.   Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "engenn5le13ob11re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "The Past Tense and Past Continuous Tense", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Simple Past tense to talk about events that are finished. </br>You use the Past Continuous to talk about events or an action that was happening at a time in the past.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Peter was taking a nap while he was waiting to get his diploma!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Peter's father took a picture of him while he was standing with the chancellor.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past Continuous\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"yawn\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"yawned\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were yawning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"scream\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"screamed\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were screaming\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"catch up\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"caught up\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were catching up\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"do\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"did\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were doing\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "The Future", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the modals <span class=\"italic\">may</span> and <span class=\"italic\">might</span> to show possibility. They have the same meaning.  Possibility means that something may or may not happen. </br>You use the modal <span class=\"italic\">will</span> to predict the future in a more certain way.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Your father might want a better photo!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I may be doing the same thing with my parents. ", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "graduation", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an event after you complete a course of study ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: My graduation from college is next week. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le13ob11aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk with old friends at graduation.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "mortar board", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a traditional hat worn to a graduation ceremony ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We threw our mortar boards in the air after the ceremony. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le13ob11aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "chancellor", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a legal official ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The university chancellor spoke at the graduation.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le13ob11aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "incredibly", "type": "name"}, {"content": "very; hard to believe", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It was incredibly difficult to do.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le13ob11aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "cap and gown", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a mortar board hat and academic style coat worn at graduation ceremonies ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Everyone put on their caps and gowns before the ceremony.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le13ob11aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Write a blog with 60-75 words talking about your future.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Say what you might, may or will do.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Explain why these are good possibilities for you. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read your blog to a partner.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I write a blog about my future.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write about what I'm doing in the future.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I read my blog aloud.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "contents": [{}], "_data": [], "id": 0, "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"image": "engenn5le13ob11re2img05.jpg", "time": "0", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"image": "engenn5le13ob11re2img05.jpg", "time": "1", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: This was an incredibly good day! </br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Camilla</span>: Everyone was screaming when we tossed our mortar boards!</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: The chancellor was yawning when he gave me my diploma!</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Camilla</span>: Your father might want a better photo!</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: I'll grab the chancellor before he takes off his cap and gown.</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Camilla</span>: I'll call you in a week. We can catch up."}, {"image": "engenn5le13ob11re2img06.jpg", "time": "15000", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: I might have a new more interesting job by then! </br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Camilla</span>: Could we meet somewhere for coffee?</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Sure. Oh. My mom is over there waving.</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Camilla</span>: Where?</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: She's got long, reddish brown hair.</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Camilla</span>: I see her. She's younger than I imagined!</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Really? Dad texted me while we were waiting to get our diplomas.</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Camilla</span>: Oh?"}, {"image": "engenn5le13ob11re2img01.jpg", "time": "33000", "id": 3, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: We're going out to dinner with family. The day is going to get much longer!</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Camilla</span>: I may be doing the same thing with my parents. </br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Well, thanks for making graduation day more fun!</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Camilla</span>: Anytime. I'll call! Bye."}], "audiosrc": "engenn5le13ob11re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn5le13ob11re2img05.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "id": 1}], "exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "I can say what I was doing when something else happened.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can compare two things. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can say what I'm doing in the future.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "How do you make choices for the future?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": "Who do you talk to?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": "What things might you consider?", "type": "Free Header Item"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"attem